      "side": 1,
      "message": "I did build virtual-device with zram as an in-tree module, and the only symbols which zram needs that aren\u0027t already in abi.stg are `pidfd_get_task` and `get_swap_device` (and `kernel_read_file_from_path` which I\u0027ll come back to). However, I\u0027m not sure if it\u0027s appropriate to put those symbols in gki/aarch64/symbols/base. The symbols in that file are extremely limited, so putting zram related symbols in seems a little strange. There are also a lot of other symbols that zram would need which aren\u0027t included in that file.\n\nI think we can just wait until someone actually takes these patches into their out-of-tree zram module to update abi.stg. Since zram uses kernel_read_file_from_path (which is on the symbol blocklist), it\u0027s currently impossible to build zram as an in-tree module. That means merging this series can\u0027t actually break any vendor builds.",
